From: ReArc Authors
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 popups with an opener get no synthetic about:blank

A window.open(url, name) popup that keeps its opener (Studio's Preview,
LeadContact's Log in with Google, any OAuth popup without noopener) stayed
on about:blank. The shell adopts the popup and installs link peek and boosts
on it at once; PageServices::EnsureInitialDocument (tab/022) then saw no
committed URL and no pending entry, because the opener's navigation of the
popup had not begun, and loaded a synthetic about:blank. That commit aborted
the opener's destination (net::ERR_ABORTED). Chrome never navigates such a
popup itself: its initial empty document belongs to the opener, which may
also script it. EnsureInitialDocument now leaves any contents with an opener
alone. noopener popups and shell-created tabs are unchanged (the former
carry a pending entry, the latter keep the tab/022 behaviour).

Bridge 0.73.0. Nothing in the C ABI changes.

Last rebased: 2026-11-16 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.100 (overlay 1cf1513cda).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/rearc_engine_entry_mac.mm b/chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/rearc_engine_entry_mac.mm
index 425c03a780..29bcfda460 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/rearc_engine_entry_mac.mm
+++ b/chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/rearc_engine_entry_mac.mm
@@ -45,7 +45,7 @@ bool HandleTerminateCancel() override {
 
 const char* ReArcEngineBridgeVersion(void) {
   CHECK([NSThread isMainThread]);
-  return "0.72.0";
+  return "0.73.0";
 }
 
 void ReArcEngineSetLifecycleCallbacks(
diff --git a/chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/rearc_services_abi.cc b/chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/rearc_services_abi.cc
index 1836ddfce7..2992d71e6b 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/rearc_services_abi.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/rearc_services_abi.cc
@@ -694,6 +694,13 @@ class PageServices : public content::DevToolsAgentHostClient,
            s->close_state() == TabSession::CloseState::kOpen;
   }
   void EnsureInitialDocument() {
+    // A window.open popup that keeps its opener has neither a commit nor a
+    // pending entry until the opener's navigation of it begins, and that
+    // initial empty document is the opener's to script. A synthetic
+    // about:blank here would abort the opener's destination (ERR_ABORTED).
+    if (web_contents()->HasOpener()) {
+      return;
+    }
     if (web_contents()->GetLastCommittedURL().is_empty() &&
         !web_contents()->GetController().GetPendingEntry()) {
       content::NavigationController::LoadURLParams params(GURL("about:blank"));
